<title>USA: Fed adds reserves via second overnight system RP.</title>
<headline>Fed adds reserves via second overnight system RP.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve added temporary reserves to the U.S. banking system for a second time on Wednesday morning via another round of overnight system repurchase agreements, the Fed confirmed.</p>
<p>At 1040 EDT/1440 GMT, the overnight bank lending, or federal funds rate was trading at 5-7/16 percent, just below the Fed's 5-1/2 percent target for the rate.</p>
<p>Earlier the Fed had added via overnight systems, as well, as experts had expected.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk 212-859-1660 ))</p>
</text>
